nted in the dataset with stronger engineered features, like `interaction_checking_employment`. Additionally, this column lacks intuitive interpretability, reducing its potential usefulness to downstream models.\ndf.drop(columns=['duration_category_encoded'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column `employment_encoded` is dropped\n# This column is a naive label encoding of `employment` that does not capture nonlinear or interaction effects, which are better represented with new features like `interaction_checking_employment` and `duration_savings_ratio`. Dropping this avoids multicollinearity.\ndf.drop(columns=['employment_encoded'], inplace=True)\n```end"]
